# Commercial UI

For user-facing UI work, load the `commercial-ui` and `frontend-ui-engineering` project skills from `.agents/skills/` (the repository symlink exposes `.claude/skills/` to Cursor).

- Ground design decisions in Brainledge's real audience, task, knowledge/context semantics, privacy boundaries, and terminology before styling.
- Prefer a coherent token/component system and semantic HTML over one-off CSS and bespoke interaction primitives.
- Treat keyboard access, focus, labels/names, contrast, responsive reflow, reduced motion, and meaningful loading/empty/error states as acceptance criteria.
- Avoid generic AI aesthetics and decorative UI that does not encode information or support a user task.
- Use the Playwright MCP configured in `.cursor/mcp.json` plus existing `packages/web` Playwright E2E coverage to verify rendered behavior. Inspect desktop and mobile together, batch fixes, then perform at most one confirmation pass.
- Do not introduce React, Next.js, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, or another frontend framework solely because an agent skill recommends it. Brainledge's current web app is Vite-based without React; framework adoption requires a separate repository decision.
- Never claim visual/browser verification unless it was actually performed.
